  "summary": "The Ismail Samani, or Samanid, Mausoleum in Bukhara, Uzbekistan, is a small, nearly cubic tomb of baked brick about 10 metres on each side, topped with a dome. Sources date it between 892 and 943, with 905 and 907 often given, and link it to the Samanid ruler Ismail, as his own tomb or as one for his father.",
